# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Constitution IX: the repository contains no personal data, ever.
# This file is the first line of that. It lands in commit one, not later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets and environment ---------------------------------------------------
# Vite loads .env, .env.local, .env.[mode] and .env.[mode].local; only the
# *.local pair is git-ignored by convention, and .env.production is a
# commit-by-habit file in that ecosystem. Ignore all of them, allow the example.
.env
.env.*
!deploy/.env.example
# NOTE: `.env` is written KEYS-ONLY by `aspire publish` and never receives a
# generated secret; it does preserve values typed in by hand. The file that
# carries RESOLVED secrets is `.env.<environment>`, written by the deploy step.
# Both are ignored. The committed key list is deploy/.env.example.
*.local
appsettings.*.local.json
secrets.json

# Aspire publish output -----------------------------------------------------
# Ignored AS A DIRECTORY, not as a file. `aspire publish` writes a .env that
# ACCUMULATES: EnvFile.Load reads whatever is already there and SaveKeysOnly
# preserves every non-empty value, so a password typed in once to make
# `docker compose up` work is rewritten into every later publish.
# The committed override lives in deploy/, NOT here.
aspire-output/
publish/

# Test artifacts ------------------------------------------------------------
# A Playwright trace carries every API response body, the rendered DOM and the
# session cookie in one zip. The hygiene job is a text scan over the diff and
# cannot see inside an archive, so these never reach git in the first place.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
*.zip
*.trace.zip

# Database ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.bak
pgdata/

